<!--
  The app's own statement about how this build was signed.

  Why a resource and not only BuildConfig: the 关于 page and anything else that
  renders text would rather read a string resource than a Java literal, and a
  resource is what a translator or a store listing can be pointed at. The
  sentence is deliberately short and unconditional — a build has exactly one
  signature, so there is no plural form and no fallback wording.

  The *truth* for a given build is `BuildConfig.SIGNING_MODE` /
  `SIGNING_RELEASABLE` / `SIGNING_NOTICE` (see android/app/build.gradle.kts),
  which the build computes from whether a real keystore was found. Use
  `BuildConfig.SIGNING_RELEASABLE` to pick between the two strings below instead
  of assuming one:

    if (BuildConfig.SIGNING_RELEASABLE) R.string.pdsh_signing_notice_release
    else                                R.string.pdsh_signing_notice_debug

  The same two sentences are also in the APK's manifest as
  `com.phonedsh.app.SIGNING_NOTICE` / `.SIGNING_MODE` <meta-data>, injected as
  manifest placeholders so resource shrinking cannot drop them.

  `android:label` is the literal "PDSH" in AndroidManifest.xml: a brand name is
  not translated, and a literal label is what `dumpsys package` prints back as
  `nonLocalizedLabel`.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="pdsh_signing_notice_debug">调试签名，不可发布</string>
    <string name="pdsh_signing_notice_release">正式签名，可发布</string>
</resources>
